necklace|neck-jewellery|NOUN|jewellery worn around the neck|A piece of jewellery designed to be worn around the neck.|vòng cổ; dây chuyền|My aunt wore a silver necklace with a small leaf-shaped pendant.|Cô tôi đeo một dây chuyền bạc có mặt nhỏ hình chiếc lá.|Countable: a necklace, necklaces. A pendant is the hanging ornament, not necessarily the whole necklace.|-
slip|lose-footing|VERB|lose secure footing|To slide unexpectedly and lose firm contact with the surface beneath your feet.|trượt chân|He slipped on the wet step but caught the handrail.|Anh trượt chân trên bậc thềm ướt nhưng kịp bám vào tay vịn.|Intransitive; slip on a surface. Slipped and slipping double the final p; slipping does not always cause a fall.|0
yard|outdoor-area|NOUN|area beside a building|An outdoor area next to a building, often enclosed.|sân|The children drew chalk patterns in the school yard.|Bọn trẻ vẽ những hình bằng phấn trong sân trường.|Countable; a yard, yards. Yard can be paved or unpaved; use depends on regional context.|0
yard|length-measure|NOUN|unit of length|A unit of length equal to three feet.|thước Anh, đơn vị chiều dài|The tailor measured a yard of blue cloth for the costume.|Người thợ may đo một thước Anh vải màu xanh lam để may trang phục.|Countable; a yard of cloth. Yard as a unit differs from an enclosed outdoor yard.|1
cotton|plant-fibre|NOUN|soft plant fibre|Soft fibres from a cotton plant, used to make thread and fabric.|bông; sợi bông|The workers sorted the cotton before it was sent to the spinning mill.|Những người công nhân phân loại bông trước khi chuyển đến nhà máy kéo sợi.|Uncountable material noun; raw cotton. The plant can be called a cotton plant.|0
cotton|cotton-fabric|NOUN|fabric made from cotton|Cloth made from cotton fibres.|vải bông; vải cotton|She chose light cotton for the summer curtains.|Cô chọn vải bông nhẹ để may rèm mùa hè.|Uncountable material noun; a cotton shirt uses cotton attributively. Fibre and fabric are related but distinct material stages.|0
exactly|with-full-precision|ADVERB|with full precision|In a way that is completely accurate or agrees fully with a stated amount or description.|đúng; chính xác|The two boards were exactly the same length.|Hai tấm ván có chiều dài bằng nhau chính xác.|Exactly the same, exactly right; put exactly before the part whose precision is emphasized.|0
